# Task workflow - follow for EVERY task

## Start
1. Read the task in `backlog/tasks.yaml` (requirements, approach, dependencies, acceptance criteria).
   Refuse to start if a dependency is not `done`; say which one.
2. Read the referenced design sections in `docs/design/CallScope_Phase3_Design.md`.
3. `git switch -c feat/<TASK-ID>-<slug>` (types: feat, fix, spike, chore, docs, test, exp).
4. `make status T=<TASK-ID> S=in_progress`.
5. State a short plan (files to touch, tests to write) before editing.

## While working
- Write/adjust tests with the code. Commit small, Conventional Commits, task ID in the footer:
  `feat(worker): add barge-in stop\n\nRefs: T-M2-05`.
- Any design decision, trade-off, spike result, or deviation from the design doc goes into
  `docs/DECISIONS.md` immediately (use the template there). Decisions that change an ADR also
  update the ADR status line.
- If you discover new work, add a task to `backlog/tasks.yaml` (next free ID, all required fields),
  do not silently expand scope.

## Before opening the PR (all must be true)
- `make ci` passes (ruff, mypy, pytest with coverage gate, backlog validation).
- `docs/CHANGELOG.md` has an entry under **Unreleased** (Added/Changed/Fixed).
- `docs/api/openapi.yaml` updated if any endpoint/contract changed; `db/schema.sql` + migration
  updated if the database changed. Contract tests updated.
- `make status T=<ID> S=in_review` then `make backlog-render`; commit `docs/BACKLOG.md`.
- PR description filled from `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`, including acceptance-criteria
  checklist with evidence (test names, run IDs, metrics).
- Append a short entry to `docs/SESSION_NOTES.md` (what was done, what is next, open questions).

## After merge
- `make status T=<ID> S=done`, `make backlog-render`.
- If it was the last task of a milestone, run the milestone-close prompt in `prompts/ceremonies.md`.

## Never
- Commit secrets, `.env`, recordings, model weights, personal data.
- Skip hooks or force-push `main`. Mark a task done with failing tests or unmet acceptance criteria.
- Claim measurements you did not run. Numbers in docs/PRs must come from real runs with IDs.
